comment_regular_data.body:
@barrettruth fair points, the comparison to other uri schemas and the possibility of a generic `editor://` schema were discussed on caleb's original issue at https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/34102

in which among the comments i put a link to my nvim terminal wrapper, [xterm-nvim](https://github.com/eylles/xterm-nvim), that implements a less sophisticated uri schema handling in the spirit of a stopgap until caleb's PR is refined and accepted.

as for caleb's PR the consensus is for it to implement the feature in a reusable, clean and extensible manner THEN further refine and extend the feature later down the line of neovim's current dev cycle.
